# Deploy Purinut Profit Monitor

Apply this only when the user asks to deploy or change production for `profit-monitor-for-docker-purinut`. Full steps are in `profit-monitor-for-docker-purinut/DEPLOY.md`.

| Item | Value |
| --- | --- |
| URL | `https://profit.sauichi.com` |
| Watch | `https://profit.sauichi.com/watch` |
| Webhook | `https://profit.sauichi.com/api/webhook` |
| Server | `root@139.180.214.152` |
| Path | `/opt/profit-monitor` |
| Origin | `ORIGIN=https://profit.sauichi.com` in the server `.env` only |

- DNS is an A record `profit` → `139.180.214.152` on Cloudflare zone `sauichi.com`, DNS only. Do not enable the proxy. Let's Encrypt HTTP-01 and TLS-ALPN need port 80/443 to reach this server.
- Do not enable zone-wide Always Use HTTPS. `https://sauichi.com` already fails at the apex origin. Do not change apex records.
- Caddy terminates TLS for `profit.sauichi.com` only. Do not restore the self-signed IP certificate or `auto_https disable_redirects`.
- Never commit or rsync `.env`. Do not put `@`, `#`, or `/` in `POSTGRES_PASSWORD`.

Update an existing deploy from `profit-monitor-for-docker-purinut`:

```bash
rsync -av --delete \
  --exclude node_modules --exclude .svelte-kit --exclude build \
  --exclude .git --exclude .env --exclude .env.local --exclude .env.* \
  ./ root@139.180.214.152:/opt/profit-monitor/
ssh root@139.180.214.152 'cd /opt/profit-monitor && docker compose up -d --build'
```

Confirm `https://profit.sauichi.com/api/health` returns healthy and `http://` redirects to `https://`. After a domain or `ORIGIN` change, tell the user to allow `https://profit.sauichi.com` in the MT4/MT5 WebRequest list.
